  "premise": "Rosalind Thornbury, a storm chaser drowning in debt to the Vane Syndicate, agrees to one last job: guide a salvage expedition into the monsoon-battered highlands using a map bought from a dying prospector with her dying breath. But the map leads to a wrecked government convoy carrying evidence of a massacre the Syndicate helped cover up, and the expedition's wealthy patron, Edmund Vane himself, intends to bury it along with everyone who saw it. When the truth surfaces mid-storm, Rosalind's ragged crew — a disgraced medic, a teenage runaway, and the prospector's estranged daughter — must choose between the payment that would save them and the justice that would damn them. In the end, Rosalind loses the map, the money, and nearly her life, but the evidence reaches the light, the Syndicate fractures, and the survivors, bound by what they endured, finally have something worth more than a clean ledger.",
  "about_author": "H. M. Kavanagh is the pen name of a former bush pilot and disaster-relief logistician who spent a decade flying supply runs into storm-struck mountain regions before turning to fiction. Kavanagh writes from a farmhouse on an unnamed coastline, drawing on real expeditions, real debts, and real storms that forgave nothing.",
